# 5. LOCAL NAVIGATION AND WORLD MAP

Phase 18 added missions, objectives and the journal. Phase 19 should improve navigation through actual spaces.

Do not build a huge open-world map application.

Create a practical **local area map / navigation system** appropriate to the existing world structure.

The player should be able to understand:
- The current area or region.
- Explored and unexplored sections where supported.
- Known routes between connected areas.
- Locked routes and their requirements.
- The current main objective.
- Relevant discovered optional points.
- Previously visited locations or checkpoints, if the campaign supports them.

### Navigation presentation

Consider a restrained map or schematic view integrated into the existing Journal/Pause/Archive interface.

The presentation may use:
- A clean 2D top-down schematic of the current region.
- Connected room/route nodes.
- A simple player-position marker.
- Main-objective marker.
- Discovered optional points.
- Locked or powered route state.
- Floor/elevation labels if the actual world supports multiple levels.

Use data derived from the real world/route model rather than hard-coded unrelated illustrations.

### Fog of discovery

Do not reveal every secret or hidden passage in advance.

A sensible default:
- Show the current region and known major routes.
- Reveal rooms or route segments after the player explores or discovers them, when this fits the level design.
- Keep undiscovered secrets hidden.
- Show locked access conditions only when the player has a legitimate clue or has encountered the lock.

### Input and UX

Inspect existing keybindings before selecting a map key.

Do not collide with:
- Weapon switching.
- Chrono Edge/Pulsecaster actions.
- Dodge or Parry.
- Echo recording/replay.
- Relay.
- Upgrade Bench.
- Ending selection.
- Existing interaction key `[I]`.

Provide a mobile-accessible map/journal entry point that does not overlap essential combat controls.

Keep the map optional and dismissible. Never force the player to navigate a map during a boss telegraph or committed combat state.

